### Summary Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Browser as Browser Client
    participant Client as AGUIChatClient
    participant Server as AG-UI Server
    participant LLM as LLM Service
    participant Storage as Session Storage

    Browser->>Client: Send message + thread_id
    Client->>Client: Build client_tool_set
    Client->>Server: POST {thread_id, messages, tools}
    Server->>Storage: Load history by thread_id
    Server->>LLM: Process with full history + all tools
    LLM-->>Server: Stream response with tool calls
    Server-->>Client: SSE stream with mixed tool calls

    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        note right of Client: Tool Separation
        Client->>Client: Check: tool_name in client_tool_set?
        alt Client Tool
            Client->>Client: Keep as function_call<br/>Add agui_thread_id
        else Server Tool
            Client->>Client: Wrap as server_function_call<br/>Register placeholder
        end
    end

    Client-->>Browser: Stream text + client tool calls
    Browser->>Browser: Execute client tools locally
    Browser->>Client: Send tool results
    Client->>Server: POST results with thread_id
    Server->>LLM: Continue with results
    LLM-->>Server: Final response
    Server-->>Client: SSE stream
    Client->>Client: Unwrap server_function_call
    Client-->>Browser: Final response
```

**Key Design Points:**

1. **Thread ID propagation** - Sent in every request, extracted from metadata or previous function calls, auto-generated if missing
2. **Full history requirement** - AG-UI protocol requires sending complete message history; thread_id enables server-side lookup
3. **Tool metadata sharing** - Client sends all tool definitions so LLM can plan across both client and server tools
4. **Streaming filter** - Client intercepts stream, checks tool names against client_tool_set, wraps server tools to prevent local execution
5. **Result unwrapping** - Server tool results are unwrapped before presentation to avoid leaking internal wrapper types

